# cli-checksums — pinned SHA-256 digests for the CLI version in bin/cli-version.
#
# Trust root: this file ships via the marketplace plugin, INDEPENDENT of the
# GitHub release assets — the launcher (bin/atlas) verifies every download
# against it and FAILS CLOSED on a missing entry or a digest mismatch.
#
# Format (identical to the release's checksums.txt):
#   <sha256 hex>  atlas-<os>-<arch>
# one line per target: atlas-darwin-arm64, atlas-darwin-x64,
# atlas-linux-arm64, atlas-linux-x64.
#
# This placeholder is accepted only while cli-pin-policy.json is in its
# one-time "bootstrap" state. The automated CLI release workflow writes both
# pin files from the exact artifacts it publishes and transitions that policy
# to "pinned" in the same generated PR. The policy cannot return to bootstrap;
# do not hand-edit a version, digest, or policy independently.
#
# TODO(release): release atlas-cli-v0.1.1 is NOT published yet — the release
# URL 404s (checked 2026-07-20), so no real digests exist. The entries are
# intentionally absent and the launcher fails closed until this file is
# regenerated from the published release artifacts. This is safe: with no
# published release the launcher's download step cannot succeed anyway.
